 ],
 "puzzleThemes": [],
 "intro": {
  "text": "The Queen's Gambit starts 1.d4 d5 2.c4: both sides push the d-pawn two squares, then White pushes the c-pawn to c4. White offers that pawn, not to give it away, but to tempt Black's d-pawn away from the centre. Here Black takes it with 2...dxc4, and you win the pawn back while you develop, that is, while you bring your knights and bishops off their starting squares. Then you castle, with the bigger share of the centre."
 },
